da9fa7a9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050221 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050221 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050221 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050221 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050221 #edb/ref 1031 "General Solutions of First-Order Linear Systems of ODEs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050221 #edb/ref 1033 3237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050221 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "3748163a-70f7-518f-9382-77b8230a6624" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165093 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186165094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165093 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186165095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165093 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186165096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165093 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186165097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165093 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186165098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165093 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165093 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165093 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4af6f441-8de0-5fd3-8a85-5a544b462091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165094 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{3}t} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{2}t}, c_{1}, c_{2} ∈ R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165094 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165094 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d9fa9552-b284-5ae3-90af-5c53bf0b2e49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165095 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{2}t} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{3}t}, c_{1}, c_{2} ∈ R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165095 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165095 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01f1d4b2-8103-5f14-b4d1-1f6df9193ba8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165096 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{3}t}, c_{1} ∈ R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165096 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165096 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1885614e-6511-5d68-89bb-33a23c4c4904" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165097 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{3}t} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{2t}, c_{1}, c_{2} ∈ R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165097 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165097 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "57253e72-5719-589e-86b0-abfcc7456d28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165098 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{2}t}, c_{1} ∈ R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165098 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165098 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "77ec0c39-01aa-537b-a144-1e5948502a91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166505 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21120" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166505 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following systems of linear ODEs are decoupled?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=7{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166505 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a19f597d-f584-57b3-9e67-cb4cea07c876" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166505 #edb/ref 1074 "A *decoupled system* consists of equations depending on only one variable, such as\n\n$$\nx'_i(t) = \\lambda_i x_i(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda_i$ is a constant. This means that we can solve each equation independently. \n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our systems.\n\n- System I is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, $x'_1(t) = 4x_1(t) + 2x_2(t)$ depends on $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t).$\n\n- System II is decoupled since its equations depend on only one variable each. Indeed, $x'_1(t) = -3x_1(t)$ depends on only $x_1(t)$ and $x'_2(t) = 7x_2(t)$ depends on only $x_2(t).$\n\n- System III is *not* decoupled because, for example, the first equation depends on $x_2(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166506 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21123" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166506 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-6{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166506 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "83ebd59d-883f-510a-9bc9-035b3088a43c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166506 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n![](images/17/17657d7db880fc0ababc24511039a9d7446952f7521e31ae3351adbb6b28ee61.png)\nthe formula for the general solution is\n![](images/44/44a286f1a4c15598038f38cdb4140534bac24caacb36f32ee4ef9cbe05b3e5e1.png)\n\nFirst, we write our differential equation in matrix form:\n\n![](images/d9/d9b9ac7fc20d076110f99476fc48d3c00c4206dc37fb2a929893fcbbb77d6526.png)\n\nSince the matrix of the differential system is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n![](images/4f/4f7cfa979200fccf811a7e0d9a633b7919b33b7740c635a921b75ad09995e700.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166507 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21124" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166507 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the initial value problem\n![](images/5c/5cc29f7492fded69b4100e10329c831cca0734a29966cd1aac2e8ad017636719.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166507 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f5136df2-fcf6-5f64-aeda-f14a91231788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166507 #edb/ref 1074 "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{1t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)})}^{t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2$ using the initial value $\\mathbf{x}(0).$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{0} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+(-1)[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying a Decoupled System of Linear ODEs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166505 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166896 #edb/ref